{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "USGS3DEP",
    "description": "USGS 3DEP regridding model — the coupler half of the usgs3dep loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.4). Exposes USGS 3D Elevation Program terrain elevation and the derived slope components (dzdx, dzdy) on the simulation's target grid for terrain coupling in EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O loader (components/earthsci_data/usgs3dep_loader.esm) as the subsystem `raw` via {\"ref\": \"./usgs3dep_loader.esm\"}. Loader fields are referenced as raw.<var> (raw.elevation, raw.dzdx, raw.dzdy) and re-exposed as model-level observed variables USGS3DEP.elevation/.dzdx/.dzdy (Pattern B), preserving the public symbol paths for downstream consumers.\n  2. Reprojection: 3DEP's native grid is geographic (longlat/WGS84, EPSG:4326), so the coordinate transform is the identity reproject (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1) — selected by convention from the loader's grid.crs.projection = 'longlat'.\n  3. Regridding (per variable, RFC §5.2): the cell-centered scalars elevation, dzdx, dzdy → conservative (area-weighted, mass-conserving) regridding, per the esm-3nc.4 migration spec (cell-centered → conservative). Declared in the `regrid` block.\n\nThis is a STATIC (time-invariant) dataset: the loader carries no `temporal` block (CONST cadence). The elevation GeoTIFF is fetched once per simulation domain; slope components are derived from it at runtime by finite differences.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:326 (USGS3DEP constructor, esm-tibb); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.4.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "elevation",
      "terrain",
      "slope",
      "regridding_model",
      "static",
      "usgs3dep",
      "dem",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.4)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "U.S. Geological Survey. 3D Elevation Program (3DEP). National Map Elevation Imagery Service. https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/",
        "url": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:1-410 (USGS3DEPFileSet, USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet, USGS3DEP constructor). Test: test/usgs3dep_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "USGS3DEP": {
      "coupletype": "USGS3DEPCoupler",
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:326\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.4). The pre-migration usgs3dep.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.USGS3DEP_data block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader is now the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/usgs3dep_loader.esm, referenced here as subsystem `raw`.\n\nUpstream constructor USGS3DEP(domaininfo) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad) from pvars(domaininfo); t_ref (reference time, s)\n  - Three observed equations via interp_unsafe:\n      elevation(t) ~ interp_unsafe(...)  from USGS3DEPFileSet\n      dzdx(t)      ~ interp_unsafe(...)  from USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet(fs, :dzdx)\n      dzdy(t)      ~ interp_unsafe(...)  from USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet(fs, :dzdy)\n  - Static dataset: DataFrequencyInfo with two time points bracketing the simulation domain (the 'static' kind means the runtime fetches once and caches)\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => USGS3DEPCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\nThese loader fields are now provided by the loader subsystem `raw` (raw.elevation, raw.dzdx, raw.dzdy) and re-exposed as the model observed variables elevation/dzdx/dzdy. (The model declares lon/lat parameters as in the pre-migration ESM; t_ref is an upstream construction detail not needed for this static loader.)\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): 3DEP's native grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (EPSG:4326), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is the identity ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1). The model does not name the ESD file; it only requires the loader's crs to be correct.\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The cell-centered scalars elevation, dzdx, dzdy → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm), per the esm-3nc.4 migration spec (cell-centered → conservative).\n\nSlope computation detail (from src/usgs3dep.jl USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet):\n  _LON2M = 40075.0e3 / (2π)      # meters per radian of longitude at equator ≈ 6378137 m/rad\n  _LAT2M = 111.32e3 * (180 / π)  # meters per radian of latitude ≈ 6367449 m/rad\n  dzdx[i,j] = Δelev_x / (Δlon * _LON2M * cos(lat[j]))\n  dzdy[i,j] = Δelev_y / (Δlat * _LAT2M)\n  Interior points use central differences; boundary points use forward/backward differences. dzdx/dzdy share the loader file_variable 'elevation' (computed from the same GeoTIFF); the slope derivation is a loader-side runtime computation, regridded conservatively here.\n\nStaticness: no `temporal` block on the loader → CONST cadence. The elevation GeoTIFF is fetched once per simulation domain. US coverage extent: lon [-180, -60], lat [17, 72] (CONUS + Alaska + Hawaii + territories); cells outside US territory receive NaN.\n\nURL construction (from src/usgs3dep.jl url() method for USGS3DEPFileSet): pixel dimensions width = min(1000, round((E-W)/resolution)), height = min(1000, round((N-S)/resolution)), where resolution = 1/3 arc-second ≈ 9.259e-5 degrees; bbox query params bbox=W,S,E,N (decimal degrees, WGS84)."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-6
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "elevation": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Terrain elevation above WGS84 ellipsoid at the model grid point (m). Sourced from the loader field raw.elevation and conservatively regridded onto the target grid. Grid cells outside US territory receive NaN. Corresponds to the upstream interp_unsafe observed equation from USGS3DEPFileSet.",
          "expression": "raw.elevation"
        },
        "dzdx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "East-west terrain slope at the model grid point (dimensionless, dz/dx in m/m). Sourced from the loader field raw.dzdx (derived at runtime from the 3DEP elevation field by finite differences with metric correction for latitude: dzdx = Δelev / (Δlon * _LON2M * cos(lat)), _LON2M ≈ 6378137 m/rad) and conservatively regridded. Corresponds to the upstream interp_unsafe observed equation from USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet(fs, :dzdx).",
          "expression": "raw.dzdx"
        },
        "dzdy": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "North-south terrain slope at the model grid point (dimensionless, dz/dy in m/m). Sourced from the loader field raw.dzdy (derived at runtime from the 3DEP elevation field by finite differences: dzdy = Δelev / (Δlat * _LAT2M), _LAT2M ≈ 6367449 m/rad) and conservatively regridded. Corresponds to the upstream interp_unsafe observed equation from USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet(fs, :dzdy).",
          "expression": "raw.dzdy"
        }
      },
      "subsystems": {
        "raw": {
          "ref": "./usgs3dep_loader.esm"
        }
      },
      "regrid": {
        "elevation": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Terrain elevation (m). Cell-centered scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap-join regridder (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm), per the esm-3nc.4 migration spec (cell-centered → conservative)."
        },
        "dzdx": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "East-west terrain slope (m/m). Cell-centered scalar (runtime-derived from elevation) → conservative regridder (esm-3nc.4 cell-centered → conservative)."
        },
        "dzdy": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "North-south terrain slope (m/m). Cell-centered scalar (runtime-derived from elevation) → conservative regridder (esm-3nc.4 cell-centered → conservative)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
